  "articleBody": "Ever notice your floor has a bit of a bounce when you walk across it? It's not just a quirky feature of your home, and it's actually a pretty common issue that can signal a few different things. Sometimes, it's just the subfloor or joists getting a little old and weak, especially in older homes. Other times, it could be water damage that's weakened the materials underneath your flooring, or even just some improper installation from way back when. It's usually a good idea to get it checked out because a bouncy floor can eventually lead to bigger problems like cracks or further structural damage. We've seen it all across Denver and the surrounding areas, from Centennial to Colorado Springs, and we can usually pinpoint the cause pretty quickly. If you're noticing this, don't just live with it! It's worth having a professional take a look before it gets worse. Give us a call at HH Remodeling LLC, and we can help you figure out what's going on and what your best options are for a solid repair.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}